      "title": "GTPv2: Add units of kbps to AMBR",
      "message": "GTPv2: Add units of kbps to AMBR\n\n3GPP TS 29.274 Section 8.7 describes the encoding for the AMBR\n(Aggregate Maximum Bit Rate) IE in GTP. The unit for this value\nis kilobits (1000bits) per second, which is not the way AMBR is\nencoded in other parts of the LTE protocol stack.\n\n3GPP TS 29.274 Section 8.15 describes the encoding for the\nBearer QOS Bit Rates (there are four of them). They are all also\nin kilobits per second.\n\nTo avoid confusion, the dissector for GTPv2 should include the\nunits when displaying the value of these Bit Rate IEs.\n",
      "author_name": "Brian C Tracy",
      "author_email": "brian.tracy33@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2024-07-25T21:34:56.000-07:00",
